  "id": "Compound::DB01438 - Gene::6334",
  "verbalization": "Phenazopyridine appears to exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving voltage-gated sodium channels, specifically Scn8a, via multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Phenazopyridine binds to Scn7a, which is involved in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, and this activity is further linked to Scn8a. Additionally, Phenazopyridine binds to Scn7a, which is also bound by Tocainide, and Tocainide binds to Scn8a, indicating a potential chain of interactions that may influence Scn8a function. The presence of multiple binding and participation relationships between Phenazopyridine and Scn8a, along with the involvement of Scn7a in sodium channel activity, suggests that Phenazopyridine may modulate Scn8a through a pathway involving Scn7a. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Scn7a as a critical mediator in the interaction between Phenazopyridine and Scn8a, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
